Circuit Breaker: Prevents cascading failures by stopping calls to failing service. States: CLOSED (normal), OPEN (failing, reject calls), HALF_OPEN (testing recovery). Like electrical circuit breaker - trips when too many failures.

```java
// Dependencies
<dependency>
  <groupId>io.github.resilience4j</groupId>
  <artifactId>resilience4j-spring-boot2</artifactId>
  <version>2.0.0</version>
</dependency>

// Configuration
application.yml:
resilience4j:
  circuitbreaker:
    instances:
      paymentService:
        registerHealthIndicator: true
        slidingWindowSize: 10 # Last 10 calls
        failureRateThreshold: 50 # Open if 50% fail
        waitDurationInOpenState: 60s # Wait 60s before trying
        permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState: 3
        automaticTransitionFromOpenToHalfOpenEnabled: true
        minimumNumberOfCalls: 5 # Need 5 calls before calculating rate

// Service implementation
@Service
public class OrderService {
  @Autowired
  private PaymentServiceClient paymentClient;

  @CircuitBreaker(
    name = "paymentService",
    fallbackMethod = "paymentFallback"
  )
  public PaymentResult processPayment(Order order) {
    // Call external payment service
    return paymentClient.charge(
      order.getCustomerId(),
      order.getTotal()
    );
  }

  // Fallback method - same signature + Throwable
  private PaymentResult paymentFallback(Order order, Throwable t) {
    log.error("Payment service unavailable, using fallback", t);

    // Return cached result, default value, or queue for later
    return PaymentResult.pending(
      "Payment service temporarily unavailable, order queued"
    );
  }
}

// Manual circuit breaker control
@Service
public class PaymentService {
  @Autowired
  private CircuitBreakerRegistry circuitBreakerRegistry;

  public void checkCircuitBreakerStatus() {
    CircuitBreaker cb = circuitBreakerRegistry.circuitBreaker("paymentService");

    CircuitBreaker.State state = cb.getState();
    CircuitBreaker.Metrics metrics = cb.getMetrics();

    log.info("Circuit Breaker State: {}", state);
    log.info("Failure Rate: {}%", metrics.getFailureRate());
    log.info("Slow Call Rate: {}%", metrics.getSlowCallRate());
    log.info("Successful Calls: {}", metrics.getNumberOfSuccessfulCalls());
    log.info("Failed Calls: {}", metrics.getNumberOfFailedCalls());
  }

  // Force open for maintenance
  public void openCircuitBreaker() {
    CircuitBreaker cb = circuitBreakerRegistry.circuitBreaker("paymentService");
    cb.transitionToOpenState();
  }
}

// Event monitoring
@Component
public class CircuitBreakerEventListener {
  @EventListener
  public void onCircuitBreakerEvent(CircuitBreakerOnStateTransitionEvent event) {
    log.warn("Circuit breaker {} changed from {} to {}",
      event.getCircuitBreakerName(),
      event.getStateTransition().getFromState(),
      event.getStateTransition().getToState()
    );

    if (event.getStateTransition().getToState() == CircuitBreaker.State.OPEN) {
      // Alert on-call engineer
      alerting.sendAlert(
        "Circuit breaker OPEN",
        "Service: " + event.getCircuitBreakerName()
      );
    }
  }
}

// Combine with Retry
@Service
public class ResilientService {
  @Retry(name = "paymentService", fallbackMethod = "fallback")
  @CircuitBreaker(name = "paymentService")
  public PaymentResult processPayment(Order order) {
    // Retry first, then circuit breaker
    return paymentClient.charge(order);
  }
}
```

Benefits: Prevents cascading failures, fast failure (no waiting), gives failing service time to recover, protects resources.

When to use: Calling external services, microservices communication, API gateway, database connections.

Bulkhead Pattern: Isolate resources for different operations to prevent one failing operation from consuming all resources. Like ship compartments - if one floods, others stay intact.

**Problem Without Bulkhead**
```java
// Shared thread pool
@Service
public class OrderService {
  @Autowired
  private RestTemplate restTemplate;

  // Uses default Tomcat thread pool (200 threads)
  public Order getOrder(String id) {
    return restTemplate.getForObject(
      "http://order-service/orders/" + id,
      Order.class
    );
  }

  public PaymentStatus getPayment(String id) {
    // Slow payment service consumes all threads
    // Now order service calls also fail!
    return restTemplate.getForObject(
      "http://payment-service/payments/" + id,
      PaymentStatus.class
    );
  }
}
```

**Solution 1: Thread Pool Bulkhead**
```java
// Configuration
application.yml:
resilience4j:
  thread-pool-bulkhead:
    instances:
      paymentService:
        maxThreadPoolSize: 10 # Max 10 threads for payment
        coreThreadPoolSize: 5
        queueCapacity: 50
        keepAliveDuration: 20s
      inventoryService:
        maxThreadPoolSize: 5 # Separate pool for inventory
        coreThreadPoolSize: 2
        queueCapacity: 20

// Implementation
@Service
public class OrderService {
  @Autowired
  private PaymentServiceClient paymentClient;

  @Autowired
  private InventoryServiceClient inventoryClient;

  @Bulkhead(
    name = "paymentService",
    type = Bulkhead.Type.THREADPOOL
  )
  public CompletableFuture<PaymentStatus> getPaymentAsync(String id) {
    // Runs in isolated thread pool (max 10 threads)
    PaymentStatus status = paymentClient.getPayment(id);
    return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(status);
  }

  @Bulkhead(
    name = "inventoryService",
    type = Bulkhead.Type.THREADPOOL
  )
  public CompletableFuture<StockLevel> getStockAsync(String sku) {
    // Separate pool (max 5 threads)
    // Payment service issues don't affect inventory calls
    StockLevel stock = inventoryClient.getStock(sku);
    return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(stock);
  }

  // Combine results
  public OrderDetails getOrderDetails(String orderId) {
    CompletableFuture<PaymentStatus> paymentFuture = 
      getPaymentAsync(orderId);

    CompletableFuture<StockLevel> stockFuture = 
      getStockAsync(orderId);

    // Wait for both (parallel execution)
    CompletableFuture.allOf(paymentFuture, stockFuture).join();

    return new OrderDetails(
      paymentFuture.join(),
      stockFuture.join()
    );
  }
}
```

**Solution 2: Semaphore Bulkhead (Lighter)**
```java
// Configuration
resilience4j:
  bulkhead:
    instances:
      paymentService:
        maxConcurrentCalls: 10 # Max 10 concurrent calls
        maxWaitDuration: 100ms # Wait max 100ms for permit

// Implementation
@Service
public class PaymentService {
  @Bulkhead(
    name = "paymentService",
    type = Bulkhead.Type.SEMAPHORE,
    fallbackMethod = "paymentFallback"
  )
  public PaymentResult processPayment(Order order) {
    // Max 10 concurrent calls
    // 11th call waits 100ms, then fails
    return paymentClient.charge(order);
  }

  private PaymentResult paymentFallback(Order order, BulkheadFullException e) {
    log.warn("Bulkhead full, rejecting payment request");
    return PaymentResult.rejected("Service temporarily overloaded");
  }
}
```

**Solution 3: Connection Pool Bulkhead**
```java
// Separate database connection pools
@Configuration
public class DataSourceConfig {
  // Orders database - large pool
  @Bean
  @Primary
  @ConfigurationProperties("spring.datasource.orders")
  public DataSource ordersDataSource() {
    return DataSourceBuilder.create()
      .type(HikariDataSource.class)
      .build();
  }

  @Bean
  public HikariConfig ordersHikariConfig() {
    HikariConfig config = new HikariConfig();
    config.setMaximumPoolSize(50); // 50 connections
    config.setMinimumIdle(10);
    return config;
  }

  // Analytics database - small pool
  @Bean
  @ConfigurationProperties("spring.datasource.analytics")
  public DataSource analyticsDataSource() {
    return DataSourceBuilder.create()
      .type(HikariDataSource.class)
      .build();
  }

  @Bean
  public HikariConfig analyticsHikariConfig() {
    HikariConfig config = new HikariConfig();
    config.setMaximumPoolSize(5); // Only 5 connections
    config.setMinimumIdle(2);
    // Analytics won't exhaust connections from orders
    return config;
  }
}
```

**Solution 4: Rate Limiter Bulkhead**
```java
// Limit rate per user to prevent one user exhausting resources
application.yml:
resilience4j:
  ratelimiter:
    instances:
      userApi:
        limitForPeriod: 10 # 10 requests
        limitRefreshPeriod: 1s # per second
        timeoutDuration: 0s # Fail immediately if limit exceeded

@RestController
public class ApiController {
  @GetMapping("/api/orders")
  @RateLimiter(name = "userApi")
  public List<Order> getOrders(@RequestHeader("User-Id") String userId) {
    // Max 10 req/s per user
    return orderService.getOrdersByUser(userId);
  }
}
```

**Monitoring**
```java
@Component
public class BulkheadMonitoring {
  @Autowired
  private BulkheadRegistry bulkheadRegistry;

  @Scheduled(fixedDelay = 60000)
  public void reportMetrics() {
    bulkheadRegistry.getAllBulkheads().forEach(bulkhead -> {
      Bulkhead.Metrics metrics = bulkhead.getMetrics();

      log.info("Bulkhead: {}", bulkhead.getName());
      log.info("Available concurrent calls: {}", 
        metrics.getAvailableConcurrentCalls());
      log.info("Max allowed: {}", 
        metrics.getMaxAllowedConcurrentCalls());

      // Alert if constantly full
      if (metrics.getAvailableConcurrentCalls() == 0) {
        alerting.sendAlert(
          "Bulkhead saturated",
          "Service: " + bulkhead.getName()
        );
      }
    });
  }
}
```

Benefits: Fault isolation (one service failure doesn't affect others), predictable resource usage, prevents resource exhaustion.

When to use: Multiple external dependencies, services with different SLAs, shared resources (threads, connections), protection against noisy neighbors.
